{# Decision template: the race and gender of a past lover nobody remembers by name. Two choice questions.
   Sent by TTLL_SexlabIntegration.SendPastLover the first time Lover's Ledger sees an actor whose SexLab
   statistics hold more encounters than the ledger and who has no spouse, lover or courting partner.
   The answer becomes a stand-in partner for those encounters (TTLL_MainController.OnPastLoverDecision).
   Option keys must match TTLL_SexlabIntegration.RaceFromKey. Context: npc_uuid. #}
{% set _npc = decnpc(npc_uuid) %}
[ state npc ]
{{ _npc.name }}, {{ _npc.gender }} {{ _npc.race }}.
{{ render_character_profile("short_inline", npc_uuid) }}
[ end state ]

[ question race choice ]
{{ _npc.name }} has had lovers in the past whose names are not recorded. Pick the race of the most likely one.
Weigh where {{ _npc.name }} lives and has lived, their own race, and the people they keep company with (`npc`).
[ criteria ]
nord: a Nord
imperial: an Imperial
breton: a Breton
redguard: a Redguard
altmer: an Altmer (High Elf)
bosmer: a Bosmer (Wood Elf)
dunmer: a Dunmer (Dark Elf)
orc: an Orc
khajiit: a Khajiit
argonian: an Argonian
[ end criteria ]
[ end question ]

[ question gender choice ]
Pick the gender of that past lover, from what `npc` says about who {{ _npc.name }} is drawn to.
If nothing says otherwise, lean toward the opposite gender of {{ _npc.name }}.
[ criteria ]
male: a man
female: a woman
[ end criteria ]
[ end question ]
